Hi Pablo,

Looks like you were making predictions in full sun (0% shade - the default setting for the minimum shade scenario, which is what is outputted to the 'soil' output in the list returned from micro_era5) but your site is in a forest. The default maximum shade is 90% and results for soil temperature under this scenario can be found in the output table 'shadsoil'. I tried running your site with the 'soil_ncep' shiny app <http://bioforecasts.science.unimelb.edu.au/app_direct/soil_ncep/> and got the plot below for 0 cm and 10 cm in 90% shade. Be sure to run at least 6 months 'spin up' prior to the time period of interest as well, so that the initial conditions (esp. soil moisture) have little impact on the predictions. It might be worth going through the vignette on the microclimate model <https://mrke.github.io/help/> if you haven't already. I'm not sure how relevant snow is to your site - does it ever snow?

All the best,
Mike

